WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.880
Hi everyone, welcome to Models and Agents for Beginners, episode 70 for June 13th, 2026.

00:00:06.740 --> 00:00:11.080
Today's AI news is pretty exciting, and I promise no jargon, let's go.

00:00:11.720 --> 00:00:17.400
Picture this, you snap a photo on your phone, but the sky feels too low or the table looks cramped

00:00:17.400 --> 00:00:23.020
on one side. Instead of cropping the shot or starting over, you now get a simple tool that stretches

00:00:23.020 --> 00:00:29.520
any edge outward by up to 25%. The phone invents what should appear in that new space,

00:00:29.940 --> 00:00:34.800
pulling from the colors and shapes already in your picture. Think of it like the way your phone

00:00:34.800 --> 00:00:40.200
guesses the next word in a text message, except this time the guess is for brand new parts of an

00:00:40.200 --> 00:00:45.880
image that never existed before. The system studies the pixels right at the edge you choose and

00:00:45.880 --> 00:00:51.740
keeps the pattern going, whether that means more blue sky with clouds or more wooden grain on a table.

00:00:51.740 --> 00:00:56.940
It checks the whole photo for clues so the new section matches the lighting and flows smoothly

00:00:56.940 --> 00:01:02.460
into the original parts. This matters for anyone who takes photos every day, because a slightly off

00:01:02.460 --> 00:01:08.240
center shot no longer has to be deleted. You can rescue group pictures that feel too tight, or turn

00:01:08.240 --> 00:01:15.440
a quick selfie into a wider scene that fills an entire screen. The feature lands in iOS 27, so once the

00:01:15.440 --> 00:01:20.440
update reaches your phone, you open the photos app, pick an image, and drag the new extend handles

00:01:20.440 --> 00:01:26.540
along any side. Watch the added space appear instantly with no extra apps or accounts required.

00:01:27.260 --> 00:01:32.820
Okay now for my favorite part of the show, where we slow down and see how something like this actually

00:01:32.820 --> 00:01:38.700
works under the hood. The deep dive today focuses on out painting, which is the technical name for

00:01:38.700 --> 00:01:44.780
extending images beyond their original borders. Imagine you are doodling on a piece of graph paper

00:01:44.780 --> 00:01:50.320
and you run out of space at the edge. Instead of stopping, you look at the lines you already drew,

00:01:50.440 --> 00:01:56.000
and continue the same pattern into the blank squares next door. The AI does something similar,

00:01:56.220 --> 00:02:01.580
but it works with millions of example photos it studied during training rather than just one drawing.

00:02:02.300 --> 00:02:07.720
First, it examines only the pixels closest to the edge you want to expand, and spots repeating

00:02:07.720 --> 00:02:14.020
patterns like sky, grass, or fabric texture. Next, it predicts how those patterns would continue if

00:02:14.020 --> 00:02:19.540
the camera had simply captured a wider view. Then it checks the entire original photo for bigger

00:02:19.540 --> 00:02:24.380
context, such as making sure shadows point the same direction and colors stay consistent.

00:02:25.100 --> 00:02:30.820
Finally, it blends the new pixels into the old ones, so the seam disappears, and the result looks

00:02:30.820 --> 00:02:36.840
like one unbroken picture. And that is basically how out painting works when your phone adds extra

00:02:36.840 --> 00:02:42.820
room to a photo. Not so scary, right? Now let's move to some cool stuff you can try yourself today.

00:02:42.820 --> 00:02:49.780
A free web tool called OwnRai Sanitize acts like a safety filter that sits between you and any chat

00:02:49.780 --> 00:02:56.060
bot. You type your question normally. The tool scans for names, addresses, phone numbers, or other

00:02:56.060 --> 00:03:01.180
private details, and it swaps them out for placeholders before anything leaves your device.

00:03:01.860 --> 00:03:06.820
Think of it like handing a letter to a friend who blacks out the sensitive lines with a marker so

00:03:06.820 --> 00:03:12.680
the recipient never sees them. This is useful when you want AI help with homework or personal

00:03:12.680 --> 00:03:19.360
planning, but do not want real information to travel across the internet. Go to the Onmiri Sanitize

00:03:19.360 --> 00:03:25.160
site, paste a test sentence that includes a fake name or address, and watch the tool replace those

00:03:25.160 --> 00:03:31.240
details in seconds. Copy the cleaned version into any chat bot and your original private information

00:03:31.240 --> 00:03:37.160
stays on your own screen. Apple is also making it clear that the next version of Siri comes from its

00:03:37.160 --> 00:03:43.100
own engineers rather than borrowing a model from another company. The company wants users to know

00:03:43.100 --> 00:03:48.640
the improvements are built in-house, which shows how several big teams are now racing to create their

00:03:48.640 --> 00:03:55.620
own smart assistance. You can watch the short clip shared by MKBHD to hear the exact wording they

00:03:55.620 --> 00:04:01.520
used. Here are a couple of quick bits to round things out. Even with powerful video AI tools,

